# rm904, the waterline guesser (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm904
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier spare
written_by claude
title the waterline guesser
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers drive=ambitious humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk guesses_every_barge_s_load_by_how_low_it_sits_in_the_water
likes river_barges a_good_bargain roast_pork wharf_evenings
dislikes river_fog nosy_questions
fears being_caught_out dying_poor
hopes a_barge_with_my_name_on_the_stern
topics prices +0.5 work +0.4 dreams +0.4 gossip +0.3 travel +0.2 faith -0.4
styles comfort=flattery gossip=keen refuse=smooth tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# talks easily and tells a little less than the truth, watches the barges on the river and guesses every load by its waterline, always has a quiet arrangement on the go, and means to own a barge one day.

words
oath! = Keel and coin | By the waterline | Low and laden
saying! = Low barge, fat purse | Everything floats at the right price | Watch the waterline, never the bargemaster
barge = a barge | a fat barge | a long barge off the river
waterline = the waterline | how low it sits
wharf = the Wharf | the wharf steps
deal = a little arrangement | a quiet bit of business | an understanding
cut = my cut | a small cut, nothing greedy
bargemaster = the bargemaster | whoever's at the tiller
someday = a barge of my own | my own barge, with my name on the stern
pork = roast pork | crackling off the spit
between = between ourselves | just between us two
whisper = a whisper | what I heard on the steps
fog = the river fog | fog on the water
dryly = Well, now | Fancy that

any
opinion @1 merchants for 2 : Merchants are only wolves who noticed the waterline before anyone else. I intend to join them.
opinion @1 watch mixed 1 : The Watch are very welcome. I keep well out of their way, purely to save them the trouble.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : The Houses got where they are by a few clever arrangements. I don't blame them. I take notes.
opinion @1 city for 2 : Every barge on the river ends up here, sooner or later. Where else would a sharp wolf live?
opinion @1 church mixed 1 : I give at chapel where it's seen. The Bright One sees the rest, I'm told, so it all comes out even.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. Lovely to meet you. Truly. | #greet#. You look like a wolf who knows a bargain.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Early on the steps is where the business is. | #greet#. Up with the barges, are we?
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Just the face I was hoping for.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit down. I've a thing to tell you, #between#. | #greet#. You're looking well. Prosperous, even.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep an eye on the river for me. | #farewell#. Think about what I said.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. We'll talk again. We always do.
line @1 react.news : Oh? More, please. All of it. | Go on. Who else knows?
line @1 react.news.new : #dryly#. That's worth knowing. | #oath#. Nobody told me that, and they ought to have.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Had it on the steps this morning. | Old news. Still, I'll act surprised for the next one.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Who gains if I believe it? | I'll weigh that one before I swallow it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. A sad business all round. | That's hard. I'm sorry, and I mean it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. I'll send something. Something small. | Good news is good for business. I'm glad.
line @1 answer.how : Doing nicely, thank you. Nicely. | #fine#. A few irons in the fire. You know how it is.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I would, but there's a prior arrangement that won't keep. | Not this time, friend. My paws are spoken for, and I never break my word. Often.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. I'll ask again when it suits you better. | No offence taken. I'll remember you said maybe.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll repay it. With interest, if I'm feeling grand. | Very decent. That goes down in my ledger, on the good side.
line @1 preclose : Well. Business calls, and it won't call twice. | I'd best be off. There's a barge due, or there ought to be.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go well. Mind how you spend it. | Go on. I'll keep your place warm.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You bargain like a lamb at a wolf market. | I've seen you pay full price. Twice. I nearly wept.
line @1 tease.return : #dryly#. And I'd sell you that remark back at cost. | Clever. I'll charge you for it later.
line @1 ack : #dryly#. | #bc_of_course#
scene low_in_the_water
when topic=work|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : There was #barge# in this morning, sitting so low the water lapped the boards. | I can tell you what's aboard any barge on the river by #waterline#. Near enough. | I lost a bet on a barge yesterday. Swore it was bricks. It was feathers.
b : What was aboard? | How do you tell? | Feathers?
a : I'd say iron. Or a bargemaster who eats well. One or the other. | The low ones are stone or metal. The high ones are wool or air. The rest's guessing. | Bales of them. I'll never live it down, so I'll stop telling it.
b : #bc_ha# | Clever. | #bc_ha#
a : I'll find out by noon. I always do. | It's a gift. Gifts aren't for handing out. #saying#. | There. You'll forget it now. Lovely.

scene fog_on_the_river
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #fog.capitalize#. You can't see a barge till it's on top of you. | I hate fog. Anything could come up the river in this and nobody'd know. | Thick as porridge out there. My whole morning's guessing, wasted.
b : It'll lift by noon. | Is that so bad? | You could guess blind.
a : By noon the good barges are unloaded and the business is done. | For me it is. For some, fog's worth its weight in silver. I wonder who. | Guess blind? I've some pride. Not much, but some.

scene quiet_arrangement
when topic=prices|work
does pre.request / go_ahead / offer / refuse / assess
a : Can I put a thing to you, #between#? | I've a small proposal. Listen first, before you say no. | You look like a wolf who'd like a little extra. Am I right?
b : Go on, then. | I'm listening. | Depends what it is.
a : I know somebody who knows somebody with a load that wants moving quietly. Nothing wicked. | A share in a guess. If I'm right about the next barge, you get a cut. | Nothing much. A word in an ear, a nod at the right moment, and #cut# for you.
b : I'd rather not. | I'll pass, thanks. | That sounds like trouble.
a : Never mind. Forget I asked. I already have. | Your loss, friend. A small one, mind. | Trouble's only trouble if you're caught. Still, no harm done.

scene steps_gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : #whisper.capitalize#: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. You didn't hear it from me. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. And I'd guess there's more to it than that. | Just between us, #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Don't pass it on. Well, not yet.
b : Is that true? | More to it? | I won't.
a : It's true enough to repeat, and that's my only test. | There's always more. I'm working on the rest. | Good. Things are worth more when fewer wolves know them.
b? : #bc_so_they_say# | #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene my_own_barge
when topic=dreams|work
does confide / react.self / assess
a : One day I'll have #someday#. You'll see it come down the river. | I've a box under the floor with every spare copper in it. It's a barge, one day. | When I'm rich I'll stand on my own deck and guess other wolves' loads for nothing.
b : Coppers add up slowly. | Under the floor? | For nothing?
a : Slowly, over a lot of years. I've time, and patience, and very few scruples. | Don't tell anyone. Not that I'd believe you if you did. | For nothing. Then I'll charge them for telling them I was right.

scene hard_times_tide
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does give.opinion / disagree / insist / ack
a : Hard times are good times for somebody. I mean to be that somebody. | Lean year. Folk sell things cheap when they're hungry. I'm only saying. | Nobody's buying, so the wolf who still has coin is king. Briefly.
b : That's a cold way to see it. | That's not kind. | Not much of a king.
a : It's an honest way to see it. Nearly. | I didn't say it was kind. I said it was so. | Briefly's all most kings get. I'll take it.
b? : #bc_maybe# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene good_times_tide
when topic=times|prices world.times=good|boom
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Barges coming in low as you like. Everyone's buying. A rising tide. | Good times. Even the bargemasters are tipping, and they never tip. | Coin's moving. You can hear it moving, like rain on a roof.
b : Good for you. | They never do. | Rain on a roof?
a : Good for all of us. Some more than others, naturally. | Never. I nearly fainted. Then I pocketed it. | The sweetest sound in the city. Better than bells.

scene crackling
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #pork.capitalize#, with the crackling still singing. Nothing better. | There's a cookshop by #wharf# that does a pork roll. I know the cook, so I pay less. | I'll forgive a wolf anything for crackling done right. Almost anything.
b : That sounds lovely. | Pay less? | Almost?
a : It is. I'd tell you where, but then it'd be crowded. | Less than you would, anyway. We have an understanding. | Almost. I'm not a saint. Saints don't get crackling.

scene keeping_clear
when topic=crime
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep well clear of the Watch. No reason. Habit. | Somebody was taken in on the steps last week. I had no part in it. None at all. | I've never done a thing I'd be ashamed of. Caught at, anyway.
b : No reason? | You're sure? | Caught at?
a : None at all. I'm the most law-abiding wolf on the river. Ask anyone I've paid. | Sure as sure. I wasn't even there. I was round the corner. | #dryly#. A slip of the tongue. I meant thought of.

scene watching_is_working
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm working. I'm watching, which is working, if you do it properly. | Busy. Three things on, and only one of them's what I'm paid for. | I'll be done here by noon, and then the real work starts.
b : Watching? | Only one? | The real work?
a : The wolf who watches knows things. The wolf who knows things eats. | The other two pay better. Don't spread it about. | The interesting kind. Never you mind.

scene green_newcomer
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Somebody fresh on the steps today. Doesn't know the prices yet. Bless. | Strangers are lovely. They're so grateful when you tell them where things are. | Somebody new in the quarter. I've introduced myself. Twice, in case.
b : You'll help them, I hope. | Grateful? | Twice?
a : I'll help them. I'm a great helper. For a small consideration. | Grateful, and generous with it. It's a lovely quality. | Once as a friend, once as a wolf with a proposal.

story the_brick_barge [topic=memories|work self.age>=25]
  : Years back I bet a bargemaster a silver piece his barge was carrying bricks, by the way it sat.
  : He laughed and said it was empty. Then he opened the hatch, and it was full of rainwater. Full to the boards.
  ask : Who do you think won the bet?
  b : Nobody, I'd say. Did you pay up?
  b[old] : The bargemaster, if he was any good.
  : I said water weighs more than bricks, so I'd won. He paid to be rid of me.

story first_copper [topic=memories|prices self.age>=18]
  : The first copper I ever made, I made selling a bargemaster his own lost rope back.
  : I'd found it on the steps. Fair and square. He never asked where.
  ask : Would you have told him?
  b : I'd have given it back free.
  b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Not if I was hungry, I wouldn't.
  : Then you're a better wolf than me, or a richer one.

rule @waterline_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere here.time=dawn|day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Low in the water, that one. Iron, I'd say. | #oath#. Riding high. Wool, or nothing at all.

rule @fog_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=fog
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #fog.capitalize#. A whole morning lost. | Can't see a thing. Somebody's doing well out of this.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#, #address#. Something I can help you with? For you, very little charge. | #greet#. You look like a wolf with a question. I've answers. Some free.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. My favourite traveller. Don't tell the others. | #topic.player#. I hoped you'd come by. I've been thinking about you. Nothing bad.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : No need for that face. I'm harmless, I promise. Mostly. | #greet#. Whatever you heard, it wasn't me.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work, I watch, and I keep my ears open. One of those pays. | A bit of this, a bit of that. Ask me about barges instead.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Think about what I said. | #farewell#. Should anybody ask, we never met. Joking.
graft resident.hub
choice What are you watching on the river? -> waterline_watch
node waterline_watch
say The barges. See how low that one sits? You can tell a load by its waterline. Low means stone or metal. High means wool, or a bargemaster who's been cheated.
mood keen
free
choice What good does knowing do you? -> waterline_use
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node waterline_use
say The wolf who knows what's coming knows what to buy before it lands. That's all business is. I'll say no more. Not for free.
choice I'll keep that in mind. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet : #greet#. Have you got anything to swap? | #greet#. You look rich. Are you rich?
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! I've got something you'll want. | #greet#. You were on my mind. Honest.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye. Remember, I was nice to you. | Bye! Come back with sweets.
line @1 react.news : Ooh. Tell me. I won't tell anyone. Much. | Really? Who said? What else?
line @1 answer.how : Good. I swapped a button for a marble. A good marble. | Fine. I'm saving up. Don't ask what for.
line @1 decline : I can't now. There's a swap on, and it's important. | Not now. Somebody's waiting for me. Somebody important.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. I'll ask again later, when you've forgotten. | Fine. Your loss.
scene pup_barge_steps
when topic=day|pastimes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sat on #wharf# all morning guessing what was on the barges. | A barge came in so low it nearly went under. I guessed rocks. | The bargemen let me count the sacks. I counted wrong on purpose. Nearly.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Did you guess right? | Was it rocks? | Wrong on purpose? Why?
b : What did you guess? | Rocks? | On purpose?
a@grown : Mostly. Once it was a goat. | It was bricks. That's nearly rocks. | To see if they were watching. They were.
a : Coal, salt, apples. All of them. | Rocks or bricks. Nearly the same. | Nearly. I'm not telling you why.

scene pup_marble_swap
when topic=pastimes|friends
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : I swapped a bent button for a blue marble. The other pup didn't know. | I've got eleven marbles now. I started with two. | I'll swap you this stone for your apple. It's a lucky stone.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's sharp dealing for a pup. | Eleven? How? | Is it truly lucky?
b : Didn't know what? | How? | Is it lucky?
a@grown : Thank you. I'm sharp. | Swapping. Clever swapping. | It is now. I've just decided.
a : That buttons aren't worth much. Shh. | Swaps. I'm good at swaps. | Very lucky. Luckier than an apple.

scene pup_father_wharf
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.father# says I've got a head for business. I think that's good. | #self.father# took me down to the river to look at the barges. I want one. | #self.father# caught me selling pebbles. It was a lot of pebbles.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : A head for business is a fine thing. | Everybody wants one at your age. | Who was buying pebbles?
b : Is it good? | A barge? | Selling pebbles?
a@grown : I hope so. I'm using it. | Not everybody. Just the clever ones. | Other pups. They were special pebbles.
a : Very good. Better than a head for sums. | A big one. With a flag. | Special ones. From the river.

scene pup_sweet_stall
when topic=food|prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The sweet stall lady gives me the broken ones if I look sad. | I paid half for a toffee because I said I only had half. | I'm saving my coppers. Sweets are for pups who don't plan.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Looking sad's an old trick. | Did you only have half? | Saving's sense.
b : Do you look sad? | Did you? | You don't eat sweets?
a@grown : It's a good trick, though. | Nearly. I had a bit more. | I know. I've got four coppers.
a : Watch. I'll show you my sad face. | Sort of. Half and a bit. | Only the free ones.

scene pup_little_fib
when topic=smalltalk|gossip
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I told a fib today. Only a little one. It worked. | Somebody asked who broke the pot. I looked at the cat. | I know a secret about somebody. I'll tell you for a sweet.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Little fibs grow, mind. | Poor cat. | Secrets aren't for selling.
b : What was it? | The cat? | What secret?
a@grown : This one won't. I'll keep it small. | It's a cat. It doesn't mind. | Everything's for selling. Somebody said.
a : Not telling. It's still working. | The cat didn't argue. | A sweet first. Then maybe.

story pup_lost_coin [topic=memories|day self.stage=young]
  : I found a copper by the river and somebody said it was theirs.
  : I asked them which side was up when they dropped it. They didn't know. I did.
  b[stage=adult|old] : Clever pup. Did you keep it?
  b : Did you keep it?
  : Yes. Then I gave it back. Then they gave me half. That's how you do it.

rule @pup_swap_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Marbles! Swaps! Good swaps here! | That barge is low. I bet it's rocks.

dlg @5 resident.hub : #greet#. Want to swap something? I've marbles. Good ones. | #greet#. You look like you've got sweets. Have you?

adolescent
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. Good timing. I've a thing to show you. | #greet#. You're looking well. Lend me a copper?
line @1 farewell.return : See you. Don't forget me. | Bye, then. Keep it quiet.
line @1 react.news : Go on. Who else knows? | Really? That's worth something.
line @1 answer.how : Doing well. Got a bit of business on. | Fine. Saving. Always saving.
line @1 decline : Can't, sorry. I've errands that pay, and that one doesn't. | Not today. I've a prior arrangement, as they say.
scene teen_message_runner
when topic=work|day self.stage=adolescent
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I run messages for the bargemen now. They tip if you're quick and don't read them. | I know which bargemasters tip and which ones shout. I only run for the tippers. | I made more this week than my first month. Running, mostly. Listening, a bit.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Don't read them, mind. | Clever. | Listening to what?
b : Do you read them? | Who tips best? | Listening?
a@grown : I never would. Not where they can see. | It's not clever. It's sense. | Things. That's all I'll say.
a : Never. Mostly never. | Not telling. Find your own. | Things worth knowing.

scene teen_caught_out
when topic=smalltalk|friends self.stage=adolescent
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I got caught in a fib. A big one. I'm still talking myself clear of it. | Somebody called me a twister. I said thank you. | I promised two folk the same thing. That was a mistake.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Talk's a long road out of a fib. | It wasn't praise. | That always comes back.
b : What happened? | Thank you? | What did you do?
a@grown : I know. I'm a good walker. | It sounded like praise. | It came back. Twice.
a : I said I'd been somewhere I hadn't. Somebody had seen me. | It sounded like a compliment. | Picked the one who pays better. Obviously.

scene teen_plans
when topic=dreams self.stage=adolescent
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I've got a plan. Barge, warehouse, then a house on the hill. | By the time I'm grown I'll have a share in a barge. A small one. | I watch the merchants. I'm learning how they talk.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Start with the barge. | A share's a start. | How do they talk?
b : All of that? | A share? | How do they talk?
a@grown : I am. Saving every copper. | It is. A small start. | Slowly, and never all of it.
a : All of it. In order. | A small share. To begin. | Like they've already won.

rule @teen_runner_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Messages run! Quick and quiet! | Low barge coming in. I'd say slate.

dlg @4 resident.hub : #greet#. Need a message run? Quick, quiet, and I never read them.
